# VideoBrief — UI

## Look

Editorial, premium, restrained, content-first on **marketing** surfaces. **App** surfaces (library, onboarding, workspace) are tool-first — paste/action prominent, scannable inventory, shared chrome. Workspace is the product centerpiece — not a SaaS card grid or chatbot shell.

## Stack

- Tailwind + **shadcn/ui** + lucide-react
- Forms: RHF + Zod + shadcn form controls
- Theme: **next-themes**, default **system** (dark-friendly tokens)
- i18n: **next-intl**, locale **`en` only** for MVP (keep message files structured)

## Component layout

```text
src/components/ui/       shadcn primitives only (add via shadcn CLI; variants OK inside)
src/components/shared/   reusable VideoBrief UI (layout, status, sync, list, form)
src/components/<feature>/ feature wiring; compose shared + ui
```

**Do not** put product-specific components in `ui/`. **Do not** add local `*Class()` maps or new semantic color combos in feature files — extend `ui/` variants or add `shared/` components.

Before duplicating Tailwind for the same pattern twice → extract to `shared/` or extend `ui/`.

## Tokens

Implement colors in `src/app/globals.css` only. Light mode: neutral white/gray app surfaces; warmth reserved for `--sync` and marketing backgrounds. Dark mode may stay warmer.

## Fonts

- Display / brand: **Newsreader**
- UI / body: **Source Sans 3**
- Avoid Inter, Roboto, Arial, system-ui as the primary brand face

## Composition

- Landing: brand-first, one clear CTA, not dashboard clutter
- Library: paste bar first, video inventory below; rows link to workspace unless failed
- Onboarding: optional YOB number, education-level select, subject chips (+ Other)
- Paste / analyze (educational): show context that will be used; up to 3 select questions; skip always allowed
- Paste / analyze (non-educational): soft disclaimer; no knowledge questions
- Workspace: video | summary/**sections** split; active section follows playback and highlights; click seeks
- Prefer document-like summary panels over chat bubbles
- Use `shared/list/panel` for bordered surfaces; not ad-hoc card class strings in features

## Motion

Intentional, minimal (2–3 purposeful motions max on marketing). Avoid glow spam and pill clusters. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Interactivity

Buttons and links use `cursor-pointer`; disabled controls use `cursor-not-allowed` or `cursor-default`.
